<title>COLOMBIA: Q1 net rises at Colombia's Coltabaco.</title>
<headline>Q1 net rises at Colombia's Coltabaco.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The first-quarter net profit of Colombia's largest cigarette maker, Coltabaco, rose to 2.67 billion pesos from 2.29 billion a year ago, the Securities Superintendency said.</p>
<p>The company, a holding of the Sindicato Antioqueno conglomerate, has a highly diversified investment portfolio and controls an estimated 60 percent of the legal cigarette market in Colombia. Contraband cigarettes have curbed the company's earnings potential, however.</p>
<p>((-- Javier Mozzo, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
